control: A reload keeps an account's token while its own current credential equals the stored one and its client is unchanged
removes: a reload always opens the stored bytes, so it drops a rotated credential whose write-back failed
packages: ./process/connections
tests: TestAFailedWriteBackIsHeldLoggedAndKeptByAReload
scheduled-count: no
integration: yes

